1
00:00:25,816 --> 00:00:27,193
Yes! Hit him!

2
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:28,986
Hit him again! Kill him!

3
00:00:29,111 --> 00:00:31,447
- Kill that son of a bitch!
- Uh, do you wanna just...

4
00:00:31,572 --> 00:00:34,408
Yeah! Break... his... face!

5
00:01:07,733 --> 00:01:09,819
Come on! Come on!

6
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:14,031
Watch the back of your head.

7
00:01:17,451 --> 00:01:19,120
You need to play harder boy,
you hear me?

8
00:01:19,704 --> 00:01:21,080
You need to play harder!

9
00:01:21,581 --> 00:01:24,417
So... you must hit
a lot of guys, huh?

10
00:01:24,542 --> 00:01:28,045
Well, I'm a cop, so it comes
with the job sometimes.

11
00:01:28,170 --> 00:01:29,547
It's only ever self...

12
00:01:29,672 --> 00:01:33,926
That is so hot. I would
love to see you hit someone.

13
00:01:34,093 --> 00:01:36,637
Oh. Uh... maybe.

14
00:01:39,265 --> 00:01:40,641
Yes!

15
00:01:44,186 --> 00:01:45,938
All right, let's fight, let's go.

16
00:02:20,723 --> 00:02:22,099
Yes!

17
00:03:20,197 --> 00:03:21,699
Charlotte Mitchell was her name.

18
00:03:21,824 --> 00:03:24,159
She was a book writer
writing a book.

19
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:27,287
Got control of the crime scene.
It's gonna be a wide suspect list.

20
00:03:27,621 --> 00:03:30,290
Get statements from all the security
guards, vendors, and attendants.

21
00:03:30,416 --> 00:03:31,792
Find out who could get backstage.

22
00:03:31,917 --> 00:03:33,377
Right. It's gonna be
hundreds, at least.

23
00:03:33,669 --> 00:03:37,047
{\an8}Look, uh, just to be clear,
I don't own this arena.

24
00:03:37,381 --> 00:03:40,718
{\an8}I simply promoted the fight.
I have no liability here.

25
00:03:40,926 --> 00:03:42,636
{\an8}What was Charlotte
Mitchell's connection to you?

26
00:03:42,845 --> 00:03:44,555
{\an8}She was writing a book
about this fight

27
00:03:44,763 --> 00:03:48,183
{\an8}about my guy, Manny Flacco,
and Rowdy Merriman.

28
00:03:48,308 --> 00:03:51,812
{\an8}She said it was a...
Microcosm of whatever. I...

29
00:03:52,688 --> 00:03:55,607
{\an8}I figured any P.R.
for my boy Manny is good P.R.

30
00:03:56,191 --> 00:03:57,568
{\an8}That's the kind of kid he is.

31
00:03:57,693 --> 00:04:00,863
{\an8}Got the initial report from the M.E...
Shot twice close range.

32
00:04:00,988 --> 00:04:02,948
Had a purse, money, jewelry all intact.

33
00:04:03,157 --> 00:04:05,117
{\an8}Estimated time of death...
8:30, 9:00 P.M.

34
00:04:05,284 --> 00:04:07,453
{\an8}That was right in the middle
of the fight.

35
00:04:08,078 --> 00:04:09,455
Excuse me.

36
00:04:09,580 --> 00:04:10,956
{\an8}When was the last
time you saw Ms. Mitchell?

37
00:04:11,498 --> 00:04:13,751
{\an8}We were supposed to sit
together during the fight.

38
00:04:14,251 --> 00:04:16,837
{\an8}She didn't show up.
Sir...

39
00:04:17,546 --> 00:04:19,214
{\an8}Why are you staring
at me like that?

40
00:04:21,049 --> 00:04:22,426
I was staring?

41
00:04:22,760 --> 00:04:25,679
{\an8}Oh, I'm so sorry.
My mind was elsewhere.

42
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:28,891
That's Charlotte Mitchell, right?
And you're, uh...

43
00:04:29,558 --> 00:04:31,685
And you're Leonard Artash, promoter.

44
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:35,147
- Let's go talk to the fighters, shall we?
- Really?

45
00:04:35,856 --> 00:04:38,066
{\an8}Well, Rigsby just told us
it wasn't a robbery.

46
00:04:38,484 --> 00:04:39,902
{\an8}We know it wasn't sexual.

47
00:04:40,027 --> 00:04:42,654
{\an8}Looks like it was in cold blood,
so not a crime of passion.

48
00:04:44,281 --> 00:04:46,742
{\an8}What's that leave us?
I'd bet your pension

49
00:04:47,034 --> 00:04:48,619
this has something
to do with the fight.

50
00:04:48,786 --> 00:04:52,206
{\an8}But Manny and Merriman were
in the cage when she was shot.

51
00:04:52,623 --> 00:04:54,541
- Are you a detective?
- No.

52
00:04:54,958 --> 00:04:56,335
Well, then.

53
00:04:56,835 --> 00:05:00,255
{\an8}Manny Flacco, you're the man.
You were fantastic in there.

54
00:05:00,881 --> 00:05:02,674
{\an8}Messed him up like
he was dog meat.

55
00:05:03,383 --> 00:05:05,093
{\an8}You're gonna be champion
of the world. You hear me?

56
00:05:05,594 --> 00:05:06,970
{\an8}Champion of the world.

57
00:05:09,139 --> 00:05:11,600
- You gotta deal with this now?
- Yes, ma'am, we do.

58
00:05:12,768 --> 00:05:14,520
What's the problem, Bea?
Who are those guys?

59
00:05:15,521 --> 00:05:16,897
They're cops.

60
00:05:17,022 --> 00:05:19,817
{\an8}Oh, come on now. Can it wait?
Let the kid enjoy his win.

61
00:05:19,942 --> 00:05:21,443
{\an8}Talk to him after he checks
in with the doctor.

62
00:05:21,568 --> 00:05:23,445
- I don't need the doc.
- Hey, better safe than sorry, right?

63
00:05:24,029 --> 00:05:25,489
Manny's got nothing
to do with this.

64
00:05:26,198 --> 00:05:27,574
Nothing to do with what?

65
00:05:27,699 --> 00:05:29,326
Charlotte Mitchell was
murdered earlier this evening.

66
00:05:29,868 --> 00:05:33,914
{\an8}- Charlotte murdered? Oh, my God.
- Stay cool. Don't get excited.

67
00:05:34,122 --> 00:05:36,500
{\an8}She was found shot to death
in a service corridor

68
00:05:36,625 --> 00:05:38,669
underneath the arena.
Happened during your fight.

69
00:05:39,253 --> 00:05:41,004
- You knew and you didn't tell me?
- Manny, come on.

70
00:05:41,129 --> 00:05:42,506
You know we're trying to protect you.

71
00:05:42,631 --> 00:05:44,007
Listen, I didn't wanna
spoil your night.

72
00:05:44,466 --> 00:05:47,135
{\an8}- Who did this?
- That's what we're looking to find out.

73
00:05:47,386 --> 00:05:50,097
{\an8}You liked her a lot, huh?
This lady, uh, what's her name?

74
00:05:50,264 --> 00:05:51,849
- "What's her name"
- Charlotte Mitchell.

75
00:05:53,767 --> 00:05:55,143
{\an8}Yeah, I liked her.

76
00:05:55,269 --> 00:05:57,187
{\an8}Everybody liked her.
She was good people.

77
00:05:57,896 --> 00:05:59,273
Yeah, she was.

78
00:06:01,650 --> 00:06:03,026
Okay.

79
00:06:04,653 --> 00:06:06,029
Great.

80
00:06:06,154 --> 00:06:07,531
{\an8}Well, thank you.

81
00:06:07,656 --> 00:06:09,741
{\an8}- Uh, where's Merriman's room?
- Oh. So we're done now, are we?

82
00:06:09,867 --> 00:06:11,243
- Oh, I'm sorry. You have some questions.
- Yeah.

83
00:06:11,368 --> 00:06:12,744
She has some questions.

84
00:06:28,635 --> 00:06:30,012
You don't wanna go back there.

85
00:06:30,888 --> 00:06:32,806
These aren't the droids
you're looking for.

86
00:06:47,779 --> 00:06:49,156
Tough night, huh?

87
00:06:49,281 --> 00:06:53,243
Uh... listen. Consolation-wise
you know what Nietzsche said.

88
00:06:57,456 --> 00:06:58,832
Man, who the hell are you?!

89
00:06:59,124 --> 00:07:00,500
You know what?
I don't even care.

90
00:07:00,626 --> 00:07:02,002
Get your butt outta here!

91
00:07:02,127 --> 00:07:04,338
- I'm CBI. I'm investigating a murder.
- Oh, you're a cop?

92
00:07:04,755 --> 00:07:06,256
- Well, not officially.
- No, man, screw murder.

93
00:07:06,381 --> 00:07:07,758
I got a robbery to report.

94
00:07:07,883 --> 00:07:09,551
That little fanny-pack Flacco
wouldn't have won dip

95
00:07:09,676 --> 00:07:11,094
if he didn't have the
stinkin' ref in his pocket!

96
00:07:11,386 --> 00:07:13,180
Son of a bitch was head-buttin'
me the whole night!

97
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:15,015
Ouch.

98
00:07:15,849 --> 00:07:17,434
- Who got murdered?
- Charlotte Mitchell.

99
00:07:18,644 --> 00:07:20,437
No kiddin'? The book writer?

100
00:07:21,939 --> 00:07:23,732
Damn. That's messed up.

101
00:07:24,858 --> 00:07:26,276
Ain't gonna be no book now,
I guess.

102
00:07:28,695 --> 00:07:30,280
They rape her as well?
She was kinda hot.

103
00:07:32,366 --> 00:07:33,742
Hello?

104
00:07:40,415 --> 00:07:44,461
Either you're a genius manipulator
concealing your complicity in the case

105
00:07:45,295 --> 00:07:49,424
or you're a... dimly lit clown.

106
00:07:50,926 --> 00:07:52,302
Which is it?

107
00:07:58,225 --> 00:07:59,601
Get back over here

108
00:07:59,726 --> 00:08:01,853
- You were right, big man.
- Say that again, you son of a bitch!

109
00:08:02,145 --> 00:08:03,897
Why don't you get back here
see what one of your mouths can...

110
00:08:04,272 --> 00:08:09,444
Hey! Hey!
Leave him alone! He's a cop!

111
00:08:15,409 --> 00:08:16,785
I'll get back to you.

112
00:08:18,412 --> 00:08:21,123
Ballistics came back.
9-millimeter weapon.

113
00:08:21,456 --> 00:08:23,542
Rifling patterns and striations
on the bullets

114
00:08:23,667 --> 00:08:25,585
indicate the gun used to kill
Charlotte Mitchell

115
00:08:25,711 --> 00:08:27,838
was also used in a murder
back in 2001.

116
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:30,007
The weapon was never recovered.

117
00:08:30,173 --> 00:08:31,758
The killer was a man
named Joe Reyes.

118
00:08:32,175 --> 00:08:33,885
Got out eight months ago.
Early release.

119
00:08:34,636 --> 00:08:36,805
Cho's still working through
suspects from the arena.

120
00:08:36,930 --> 00:08:38,515
Take Rigsby and talk to Reyes.

121
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,017
Find out what happened
to that gun.

122
00:08:40,308 --> 00:08:43,770
- I'm gonna go talk to the victim's father.
- Rigsby's... busy.

123
00:08:44,521 --> 00:08:45,897
With what?

124
00:08:46,023 --> 00:08:47,858
- Mr. LaRoche is interviewing him.
- Oh?

125
00:08:48,734 --> 00:08:53,071
A man named Todd Johnson
was murdered while in CBI custody.

126
00:08:53,196 --> 00:08:55,615
Yes. Cop killer,
burned to death in his cell.

127
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,369
I just wanted to get your opinion
on some things.

128
00:09:00,412 --> 00:09:03,290
You were an arson investigator
before coming to CBI, right?

129
00:09:03,623 --> 00:09:07,836
- Yeah, in San Diego.
- Yeah. Are you familiar with...

130
00:09:09,337 --> 00:09:12,966
- Pyrophoric igniters?
- Sure. Liquid or solid?

131
00:09:13,383 --> 00:09:17,429
Used in conjunction
with a xylene accelerant?

132
00:09:17,971 --> 00:09:19,639
- Overkill, I'd say.
- Really?

133
00:09:20,390 --> 00:09:23,268
And the fire safety system
here in CBI...

134
00:09:24,811 --> 00:09:26,813
Easy to access and deactivate?

135
00:09:27,105 --> 00:09:28,982
Top-of-the-line E.S.F.R system?
No.

136
00:09:29,107 --> 00:09:30,484
Bypassing that took real know-how.

137
00:09:31,943 --> 00:09:34,529
You could deactivate it,
couldn't you?

138
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:36,907
Yes, I could.

139
00:09:38,492 --> 00:09:39,868
Are you accusing me?

140
00:09:41,620 --> 00:09:42,996
Are you confessing?

141
00:09:48,960 --> 00:09:52,631
Your father
is Steven Robert Rigsby.

142
00:09:53,381 --> 00:09:54,758
Yes, he is.

143
00:09:54,883 --> 00:09:56,259
What does he got to do
with the investigation?

144
00:09:56,426 --> 00:10:00,347
Used to be affiliated with the Iron Gods
motorcycle gang, yes?

145
00:10:00,639 --> 00:10:02,015
Well, you know he was.

146
00:10:02,140 --> 00:10:03,975
Yes, I have his sheet here.

147
00:10:06,103 --> 00:10:08,271
Robbery.
Narcotics.

148
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:10,357
Assault.

149
00:10:10,732 --> 00:10:14,611
Manslaughter. Quite the rascal.

150
00:10:14,778 --> 00:10:16,404
Look, I have nothing to do
with my father.

151
00:10:16,988 --> 00:10:19,950
Nothing at all?
No card at Christmas?

152
00:10:20,075 --> 00:10:22,035
Nope. We don't talk.
I don't know where he is.

153
00:10:23,203 --> 00:10:24,579
LaRoche.

154
00:10:24,704 --> 00:10:26,289
You're supposed to inform me
when you talk to one of my people.

155
00:10:26,873 --> 00:10:28,667
That's not a right.

156
00:10:29,251 --> 00:10:31,545
That's a courtesy we extend
on occasion.

157
00:10:31,962 --> 00:10:35,006
Well, in the future I'd like you
to extend that courtesy to me.

158
00:10:39,761 --> 00:10:42,931
Thank you, agent Rigsby.
That should do it.

159
00:10:49,855 --> 00:10:52,732
"Shall he lead"

160
00:10:52,899 --> 00:10:56,862
"Every foe is vanquished"

161
00:10:57,070 --> 00:11:00,657
"And Christ is lord indeed"

162
00:11:00,782 --> 00:11:02,492
- Amen, amen.
- Amen.

163
00:11:02,617 --> 00:11:05,328
Welcome. We have newcomers,
brothers and sisters.

164
00:11:05,453 --> 00:11:06,830
Make 'em feel welcome.

165
00:11:10,041 --> 00:11:11,418
Joseph Reyes?

166
00:11:16,256 --> 00:11:19,634
My gun. A woman
was killed with my gun?

167
00:11:19,926 --> 00:11:21,595
Same one you used back in 2001.

168
00:11:23,972 --> 00:11:26,474
So you just cannot escape
the sins of the past.

169
00:11:27,726 --> 00:11:30,645
All you can do is ask the lord's guidance
and you know, keep on, man.

170
00:11:30,896 --> 00:11:33,940
- Did you know Charlotte Mitchell?
- No, ma'am, I did not

171
00:11:34,191 --> 00:11:35,650
and I don't have that gun
anymore either.

172
00:11:35,775 --> 00:11:37,152
Got rid of it back
when you shot that guy?

173
00:11:38,904 --> 00:11:40,280
What did you do with it?

174
00:11:40,405 --> 00:11:41,990
I gave it to a lady friend
of mine at the time.

175
00:11:42,365 --> 00:11:44,618
- What did she do with it?
- That I don't know.

176
00:11:44,743 --> 00:11:46,119
I haven't seen her since my arrest.

177
00:11:46,369 --> 00:11:47,746
What was the lady's name?

178
00:11:47,871 --> 00:11:49,998
Uh... Dawn. Dawn May.

179
00:11:50,624 --> 00:11:52,334
- Address?
- Don't know.

180
00:11:53,084 --> 00:11:54,669
Like I said, I didn't look for her
when I got out.

181
00:11:55,378 --> 00:12:00,008
After finding my faith, I realize I had
to turn my back on all my evil ways

182
00:12:00,133 --> 00:12:02,510
and all the people that could possibly
lead me back there.

183
00:12:04,012 --> 00:12:05,388
All right. Thanks for your time.

184
00:12:07,807 --> 00:12:09,851
Why did you kill that man
back in 2001?

185
00:12:10,018 --> 00:12:11,394
If you don't mind my asking.

186
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,316
I don't know, ma'am.

187
00:12:17,442 --> 00:12:18,818
It was foolishness.

188
00:12:20,028 --> 00:12:22,405
Look, I did a lot of bad
things back in the day

189
00:12:23,531 --> 00:12:25,158
and that was just the one
they caught me for.

190
00:12:27,619 --> 00:12:28,995
This is God's plan.

191
00:12:38,255 --> 00:12:41,216
{\an8}- "Here it is. I found it."
- "Good, good, good, good. Okay."

192
00:12:41,549 --> 00:12:43,051
- "Hold it up."
- "Dad."

193
00:12:43,176 --> 00:12:46,596
"No, come on. Hold it up.
Higher, higher, higher. Okay."

194
00:12:46,721 --> 00:12:48,098
"It's just a town hall report."

195
00:12:48,390 --> 00:12:51,351
"No, it's your first
newspaper article..."

196
00:12:56,731 --> 00:12:58,108
She was a good girl.

197
00:12:59,567 --> 00:13:00,944
A fine human being.

198
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,031
We're sorry for your loss,
Mr. Mitchell.

199
00:13:06,032 --> 00:13:07,409
Thank you.

200
00:13:08,368 --> 00:13:10,328
Would you mind terribly if I
just took a little look around?

201
00:13:11,121 --> 00:13:12,706
Uh, no, uh, not at all.

202
00:13:12,956 --> 00:13:17,335
The kitchen is, uh, there,
and her office is this way.

203
00:13:20,922 --> 00:13:22,299
These...

204
00:13:23,717 --> 00:13:25,176
Are her notebooks.

205
00:13:26,511 --> 00:13:27,887
She kept good notes.

206
00:13:28,805 --> 00:13:30,181
I taught her that.

207
00:13:32,767 --> 00:13:37,022
I apologized to her only last week
teaching her a dying profession.

208
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:40,400
Journalism's dying, you know.

209
00:13:43,028 --> 00:13:44,404
All this...

210
00:13:45,613 --> 00:13:46,990
Internet.

211
00:13:48,116 --> 00:13:50,201
Uh, maybe we should go
in the living room, Mr. Mitchell.

212
00:13:51,119 --> 00:13:54,456
- Uh, yeah.
- I'll take this.

213
00:13:57,208 --> 00:13:58,585
I'll be right there.

214
00:13:59,002 --> 00:14:00,670
Just try and relax, sir.

215
00:14:04,299 --> 00:14:05,675
Can I get you something to drink,
Mr. Mitchell?

216
00:14:05,800 --> 00:14:07,177
Some water, maybe?

217
00:14:07,302 --> 00:14:09,512
Yeah. That would be very nice,
thank you.

218
00:14:19,272 --> 00:14:20,648
"It's newspaper articles."

219
00:14:20,774 --> 00:14:22,359
"No, I've been published
in real newspapers before."

220
00:14:22,901 --> 00:14:25,820
- "Those were not real newspapers."
- "Yes, they were so!"

221
00:14:25,945 --> 00:14:28,490
"No, they weren't.
No, okay. All right, all right."

222
00:14:28,615 --> 00:14:29,991
"Now I want you to read from it."

223
00:14:32,243 --> 00:14:33,787
- "Come on. Read from it."
- "I'm reading it."

224
00:14:35,413 --> 00:14:37,832
"Out loud! Go on!"

225
00:14:38,166 --> 00:14:40,794
"Grove Park interim
mayor Joyce Franklin"

226
00:14:40,919 --> 00:14:43,922
"presided today over the opening
of a brand-new senior center"

227
00:14:44,047 --> 00:14:46,716
"named for retiring
councilman Sam Chapin."

228
00:14:47,759 --> 00:14:49,135
"Uh... there."

229
00:14:50,178 --> 00:14:52,680
"Read the whole thing. Come on."

230
00:14:53,014 --> 00:14:55,266
"The center will serve
the Grove Park community"

231
00:14:55,392 --> 00:14:57,394
"and the surrounding areas..."

232
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:01,898
Jane! Jane! Get in here!

233
00:15:03,733 --> 00:15:05,193
Heart attack. Ambulance.

234
00:15:07,445 --> 00:15:09,447
Mr. Mitchell, stay with me.

235
00:15:18,679 --> 00:15:20,056
Thanks.

236
00:15:20,806 --> 00:15:22,767
"Flacco is continuing
to pummel Merriman..."

237
00:15:23,559 --> 00:15:26,687
The doctors say Tom Mitchell
had a major cardiac arrest.

238
00:15:27,255 --> 00:15:28,631
I could have told them that.

239
00:15:28,756 --> 00:15:30,925
They were able to stabilize him,
but he's still unconscious.

240
00:15:31,050 --> 00:15:32,927
They're gonna keep him in I.C.U.
until he wakes up.

241
00:15:33,511 --> 00:15:34,887
Poor man.

242
00:15:36,806 --> 00:15:38,766
- Went down and stayed down.
- Oh, yeah.

243
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,227
But I've been looking through
Mitchell's notebooks.

244
00:15:41,602 --> 00:15:43,688
Aside from a whole bunch
of stuff about the dangers

245
00:15:43,813 --> 00:15:45,982
of mixed martial arts
fighting and blood markers

246
00:15:46,274 --> 00:15:47,984
she was looking
for a fight fixing angle.

247
00:15:48,484 --> 00:15:50,903
- What do you think?
- Merriman took a fall?

248
00:15:51,529 --> 00:15:53,948
Ah, I can't see it.
It's worth killing over, though.

249
00:15:54,449 --> 00:15:56,200
A lot of money to be made
on a sure thing.

250
00:15:56,826 --> 00:15:58,661
We should talk to the promoter,
Artash

251
00:15:58,870 --> 00:16:00,455
see what he has to say
about fight fixing.

252
00:16:08,963 --> 00:16:10,339
Mr. Artash?

253
00:16:12,258 --> 00:16:13,634
All right, 60/40 split.

254
00:16:14,177 --> 00:16:15,928
And an option
for his next three fights.

255
00:16:16,929 --> 00:16:20,016
Hey, alternatively,
go eat a shoelace.

256
00:16:20,641 --> 00:16:24,145
Hey. I want the deal done by Friday.
Call me back.

257
00:16:26,772 --> 00:16:28,149
We got it!

258
00:16:28,274 --> 00:16:30,359
Manny fights for the title,
six months' time.

259
00:16:30,818 --> 00:16:32,528
$2 million purse.

260
00:16:33,321 --> 00:16:34,697
Can I pick 'em or what?

261
00:16:35,406 --> 00:16:36,782
You see that kid
with the long hair?

262
00:16:36,949 --> 00:16:39,160
He's gonna be my next champion.
Mark my words.

263
00:16:39,285 --> 00:16:40,745
Fight fixing...
What can you tell us about it?

264
00:16:41,162 --> 00:16:42,538
No, that doesn't happen.

265
00:16:42,914 --> 00:16:47,043
The board finds out everyone involved
is done forever.

266
00:16:47,210 --> 00:16:49,253
And you need a fighter
willing to take a dive

267
00:16:49,587 --> 00:16:51,047
- which Merriman isn't.
- No?

268
00:16:51,714 --> 00:16:53,090
Egotistical jerk like him?

269
00:16:53,466 --> 00:16:54,842
Come on!

270
00:16:55,551 --> 00:16:57,303
Stick the jab and shoot it.

271
00:16:58,137 --> 00:16:59,514
Stick and shoot!

272
00:17:02,016 --> 00:17:03,392
Get off the ropes!

273
00:17:06,062 --> 00:17:07,730
Your fighter looks
bigger and stronger.

274
00:17:07,855 --> 00:17:10,191
- Shouldn't he be winning?
- He's slower and dumber.

275
00:17:16,572 --> 00:17:18,950
You're Floyd Benton, aren't you?
Didn't you train Manny Flacco?

276
00:17:19,242 --> 00:17:21,619
Used to, until he got too big
and smart to learn.

277
00:17:22,411 --> 00:17:24,705
Come on, son of a bitch.
Stick it! Move! Come on!

278
00:17:28,376 --> 00:17:29,752
Police officer.

279
00:17:30,294 --> 00:17:31,671
How'd you know?

280
00:17:31,796 --> 00:17:33,172
Police and fine women always
think they got a right

281
00:17:33,297 --> 00:17:35,841
to be wherever they're at,
and you ain't no fine woman.

282
00:17:38,427 --> 00:17:39,804
I'm here about Charlotte Mitchell.

283
00:17:40,471 --> 00:17:42,098
Yeah. Poor girl.

284
00:17:43,516 --> 00:17:44,892
You think it was about the fight?

285
00:17:45,601 --> 00:17:46,978
What do you think?

286
00:17:47,228 --> 00:17:49,605
I think if it wasn't about the fight
you wouldn't even be here.

287
00:17:50,231 --> 00:17:53,734
What aspect of the fight do you
think would motivate murder?

288
00:17:57,446 --> 00:17:58,823
You're the detective.

289
00:17:58,948 --> 00:18:00,324
What, am I supposed to do
your job for you?

290
00:18:01,742 --> 00:18:04,370
What if I do your job for you?
Is that a fair exchange?

291
00:18:05,538 --> 00:18:06,914
Shoot.

292
00:18:07,039 --> 00:18:08,416
Artash's prospect has a tell.

293
00:18:08,874 --> 00:18:11,586
He taps his forehead before
he throws a right uppercut.

294
00:18:11,711 --> 00:18:14,714
When he does that, your guy should
step to the right and throw a hook.

295
00:18:19,468 --> 00:18:21,012
Damn, if you ain't almost correct.

296
00:18:22,972 --> 00:18:24,348
You got a good eye.

297
00:18:24,473 --> 00:18:26,642
Well, thank you.
Now it's your turn.

298
00:18:27,268 --> 00:18:29,270
Charlotte Mitchell...
Who killed her?

299
00:18:30,229 --> 00:18:33,107
Don't know. But I will say this.

300
00:18:33,232 --> 00:18:35,359
There's more to Manny Flacco
than meets the eye.

301
00:18:37,612 --> 00:18:40,239
- And what's that?
- Just a vibe I get.

302
00:18:40,948 --> 00:18:42,450
Does that vibe have anything to do

303
00:18:42,575 --> 00:18:44,327
with the fact that he fired you
as his trainer?

304
00:18:47,663 --> 00:18:49,040
I'm a bigger man than that.

305
00:18:50,875 --> 00:18:52,835
Okay, listen up. Come here.
Come here, come here, come here.

306
00:18:54,503 --> 00:18:55,880
Listen, the man there...

307
00:19:01,135 --> 00:19:02,970
There she is...
Joe Reyes' old girlfriend.

308
00:19:03,554 --> 00:19:05,890
Keep on going.
All right. Come on now.

309
00:19:06,140 --> 00:19:07,558
- Keep movin'.
- Dawn May?

310
00:19:08,726 --> 00:19:10,478
- We need to talk.
- What's this about?

311
00:19:10,728 --> 00:19:12,146
You remember a guy
named Joe Reyes?

312
00:19:12,396 --> 00:19:13,898
We need to know what happened
to a gun he gave you.

313
00:19:14,982 --> 00:19:16,359
Could you guys keep it down?

314
00:19:16,609 --> 00:19:19,236
People around here might get upset
they knew about my past business.

315
00:19:19,362 --> 00:19:20,738
The gun...
What'd you do with it?

316
00:19:21,697 --> 00:19:24,700
I gave it to my cousin Bobby.
I don't know what he did with it.

317
00:19:24,825 --> 00:19:26,202
Where's your cousin Bobby?

318
00:19:26,410 --> 00:19:28,412
Dead. Got blown up in Iraq.

319
00:19:29,747 --> 00:19:31,624
- Excuse me.
- What's this all about?

320
00:19:31,832 --> 00:19:33,292
- Hello?
- Am I in trouble?

321
00:19:34,585 --> 00:19:36,754
Agent Rigsby,
this is J.J. LaRoche.

322
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,674
Where are you?
We need to talk more.

323
00:19:40,049 --> 00:19:42,343
- I'm working a case.
- "When are you coming back in?"

324
00:19:42,635 --> 00:19:44,136
Well, I couldn't say.
It's an active case.

325
00:19:44,428 --> 00:19:46,430
I could agent Lisbon
to bring you back.

326
00:19:46,972 --> 00:19:48,349
"Should I do that?"

327
00:19:49,392 --> 00:19:50,768
I'll be there in an hour.

328
00:19:55,272 --> 00:19:56,816
Two kids I'm trying to raise right

329
00:19:56,941 --> 00:19:58,484
who don't know
the kind of life I used to lead.

330
00:19:58,859 --> 00:20:00,903
Ma'am, we won't speak to your children
about this, unless we need to.

331
00:20:01,070 --> 00:20:02,446
- You ready?
- Yeah.

332
00:20:02,571 --> 00:20:04,073
- Thank you, ma'am. We'll be in touch.
- Thank you.

333
00:20:07,368 --> 00:20:09,537
Says she was at a parent-teacher
conference the night before last.

334
00:20:09,704 --> 00:20:11,080
Should be easy to check.

335
00:20:12,915 --> 00:20:15,751
- Anything wrong? Who called?
- Nothing. Nobody.

336
00:20:20,673 --> 00:20:22,883
You said there had
been no contact.

337
00:20:23,426 --> 00:20:26,637
But phone records show six
phone calls from your father

338
00:20:26,762 --> 00:20:29,306
between June and July of 2008.

339
00:20:29,807 --> 00:20:31,183
What does this have to do with someone

340
00:20:31,308 --> 00:20:32,768
burning a cop killer to death
here in CBI?

341
00:20:33,394 --> 00:20:34,770
Nothing... directly.

342
00:20:35,438 --> 00:20:38,941
- But it does speak to character.
- You're questioning my character?

343
00:20:40,443 --> 00:20:47,742
Did you know there are criminological studies
that posit criminality as a heritable trait?

344
00:20:48,367 --> 00:20:50,995
Like eye color
or a baritone voice.

345
00:20:51,203 --> 00:20:52,580
What?

346
00:20:52,705 --> 00:20:56,459
I just mean... it may not
be your fault, agent Rigsby.

347
00:20:57,460 --> 00:21:01,255
You may simply be predisposed
to criminal behavior

348
00:21:02,423 --> 00:21:03,799
scientifically speaking.

349
00:21:03,924 --> 00:21:07,094
Look, my father called me
about a mix-up with his parole officer.

350
00:21:07,261 --> 00:21:08,804
Was I supposed to
ignore him? Hang up?

351
00:21:09,096 --> 00:21:12,600
And did you forget that conversation
or you just chose not to speak of it?

352
00:21:12,767 --> 00:21:14,143
I forgot.

353
00:21:16,937 --> 00:21:19,148
Are we done here?
I think we're done.

354
00:21:30,451 --> 00:21:31,911
Hey. I got something.

355
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:35,456
A security guard had a run-in
with Charlotte Mitchell before the fight.

356
00:21:35,748 --> 00:21:37,416
She was trying
to get into the dressing room area.

357
00:21:37,750 --> 00:21:40,586
Didn't have the right kind of access laminate
so he wouldn't let her in.

358
00:21:41,045 --> 00:21:43,380
She got agitated, made a scene
and he threw her out.

359
00:21:43,547 --> 00:21:46,300
- This was at approximately 6:30.
- 6:30?

360
00:21:46,884 --> 00:21:49,386
And that puts her in the arena an hour
before the M.E.'s estimate.

361
00:21:49,678 --> 00:21:52,681
Yep, and that means Flacco and Merriman
both had opportunity.

362
00:21:52,848 --> 00:21:54,225
They're suspects, too.

363
00:21:54,350 --> 00:21:55,851
Bring 'em both in. See what they
have to say under questioning.

364
00:21:56,352 --> 00:21:57,728
Okay.

365
00:22:05,611 --> 00:22:07,988
Mr. Merriman, your associates
are gonna have to wait outside.

366
00:22:08,405 --> 00:22:10,032
- Oh, they're cool.
- They're cool outside.

367
00:22:12,117 --> 00:22:14,912
Hey, Flacco, you little punk!
You used plaster wraps, didn't you?

368
00:22:15,287 --> 00:22:17,206
I know a little punk like
you don't hit that hard!

369
00:22:17,748 --> 00:22:19,792
Mr. and Mrs. Flacco,
why don't we talk in my office?

370
00:22:20,417 --> 00:22:21,794
Come on, babe.

371
00:22:21,919 --> 00:22:23,921
Oh, now you running away, Manny?
Just like you did in the cage, huh?

372
00:22:24,839 --> 00:22:26,549
Two million people saw me
kick your butt.

373
00:22:26,757 --> 00:22:28,676
- Live with it.
- Oh, hell, no. Come on!

374
00:22:29,510 --> 00:22:31,512
Control yourselves, both of you.

375
00:22:31,679 --> 00:22:34,265
Look, either of you try anything
and I'm gonna put you in cuffs.

376
00:22:34,390 --> 00:22:36,642
So let's just calm down
and get back to business.

377
00:22:41,480 --> 00:22:42,857
I think you like
getting beaten up.

378
00:22:43,566 --> 00:22:45,359
A little masochistic
streak there, huh?

379
00:22:48,070 --> 00:22:49,446
Thanks for that. Thanks.

380
00:22:49,572 --> 00:22:53,659
- Break it up, guys! That is enough!
- Hey! Take it easy, take it easy.

381
00:22:55,411 --> 00:22:57,621
Come on! Knock it off!

382
00:22:58,622 --> 00:22:59,999
Knock it off!

383
00:23:04,418 --> 00:23:05,794
What the hell is going on here?

384
00:23:05,919 --> 00:23:07,296
Do you people even
know what you're doing?

385
00:23:07,421 --> 00:23:08,797
- Sit down, Mr. Lima.
- No!

386
00:23:08,922 --> 00:23:10,340
Not until you tell me why you're setting
Manny up to get jumped.

387
00:23:10,632 --> 00:23:12,718
Mr. Lima, how we conduct interviews
is not your concern.

388
00:23:12,843 --> 00:23:14,678
It is if it endangers my fighter.

389
00:23:14,845 --> 00:23:16,263
Manny shouldn't have been
called in here anyway.

390
00:23:16,388 --> 00:23:17,764
He's grieving for Charlotte.

391
00:23:17,890 --> 00:23:19,266
We just need to ask him
a few questions.

392
00:23:19,391 --> 00:23:20,767
- Now, please, take a seat.
- Why?

393
00:23:20,893 --> 00:23:22,269
I mean, you got the man
you want already.

394
00:23:22,394 --> 00:23:23,854
- You mean Rowdy Merriman?
- You saw him.

395
00:23:24,187 --> 00:23:25,856
He doesn't like it
when he doesn't get what he wants

396
00:23:25,981 --> 00:23:27,900
and he didn't get what
he wanted from Charlotte.

397
00:23:28,025 --> 00:23:29,943
- And what did he want?
- Guess.

398
00:23:32,362 --> 00:23:34,615
Nah, I didn't kill the writer lady.
Why would I?

399
00:23:35,407 --> 00:23:36,783
I've looked at your rap sheet.

400
00:23:37,034 --> 00:23:38,577
There's a history of violence
against women.

401
00:23:39,494 --> 00:23:41,663
Man, if I slap a bitch,
it's cause she asked for it.

402
00:23:42,414 --> 00:23:44,374
Bitches like to get slapped.
Don't ask me why.

403
00:23:44,499 --> 00:23:47,002
- Did Charlotte Mitchell ask for it?
- No, she didn't.

404
00:23:47,336 --> 00:23:48,879
But I asked her, though, you know?

405
00:23:50,005 --> 00:23:52,841
You know, she was like... "Ew!"
You know, I disgusted her, man.

406
00:23:53,842 --> 00:23:55,218
Nice, clean, college lady.

407
00:23:55,344 --> 00:23:56,970
She rejected you.
How'd that make you feel?

408
00:23:57,804 --> 00:24:00,474
Like I had to call another bitch
to break me off a piece, which I did.

409
00:24:02,184 --> 00:24:03,769
Now she was researching
you and Flacco.

410
00:24:04,603 --> 00:24:05,979
Maybe she found out
something about you

411
00:24:06,104 --> 00:24:07,481
you didn't want anybody to know.

412
00:24:07,606 --> 00:24:09,107
Man, you know what?
I got nothin' to hide.

413
00:24:09,399 --> 00:24:11,276
I'm straight up thug,
and I'm proud of it.

414
00:24:11,860 --> 00:24:13,987
You know, what they gonna say about me
that ain't already been said, huh?

415
00:24:14,947 --> 00:24:17,532
Nah. Little Mr. Perfect...
He's the one got secrets to be hidin'.

416
00:24:17,950 --> 00:24:19,326
Flacco... What's he got to hide?

417
00:24:19,993 --> 00:24:21,995
I mean, he was knocking boots
with that writer lady, for one

418
00:24:22,120 --> 00:24:24,456
- dogging on that nasty little wife of his.
- You got proof of that?

419
00:24:25,082 --> 00:24:27,960
Proof, man. Ask the punk, dude.
He'll be like...

420
00:24:33,131 --> 00:24:34,508
Yeah, go ask him.

421
00:24:39,346 --> 00:24:40,722
Mr. Flacco?

422
00:24:41,431 --> 00:24:43,433
Do you want your wife present
during our interview?

423
00:24:43,892 --> 00:24:45,268
Normally, we do this alone.

424
00:24:45,811 --> 00:24:47,896
I need her here.
I got no secrets from Bea.

425
00:24:48,563 --> 00:24:51,274
Okay. What was your relationship
with Charlotte Mitchell?

426
00:24:51,817 --> 00:24:54,361
She was writing a book about
me and Rowdy, about the fight.

427
00:24:54,903 --> 00:24:57,614
- Which started when?
- Since I started training for the fight.

428
00:24:58,198 --> 00:24:59,574
Six months ago.

429
00:24:59,908 --> 00:25:01,868
And how about
when you weren't training?

430
00:25:03,370 --> 00:25:05,414
- What does that mean?
- Don't act dumb, Manny.

431
00:25:05,539 --> 00:25:06,915
She wants to know if you were
sleeping with her.

432
00:25:07,040 --> 00:25:09,626
- What? No.
- Look at me when you say that.

433
00:25:09,876 --> 00:25:14,423
- Honey, I wasn't sleeping with her.
- "Honey"? Please.

434
00:25:15,090 --> 00:25:16,675
- So he's sleeping with her? So what?
- Bea...

435
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:18,218
No. I don't wanna hear it now.

436
00:25:19,344 --> 00:25:22,723
We've been together since I'm 13
married since 17, 4 kids.

437
00:25:22,848 --> 00:25:24,224
You think I don't know
what's going on?

438
00:25:24,433 --> 00:25:25,976
He's a professional athlete.

439
00:25:26,768 --> 00:25:29,104
I blame it on the women.
Men don't know any better.

440
00:25:29,229 --> 00:25:30,605
- Baby, I never s...
- And you know what?

441
00:25:30,731 --> 00:25:32,691
Manny's good.
He doesn't go all crazy.

442
00:25:32,858 --> 00:25:36,486
But we do have the nurse
at the physio clinic

443
00:25:36,820 --> 00:25:39,239
the two waitresses in Vegas,
the girl at Len's club...

444
00:25:39,364 --> 00:25:41,742
Where were you the night
of the fight, Ms. Flacco?

445
00:25:42,617 --> 00:25:43,994
Backstage.

446
00:25:44,119 --> 00:25:46,079
I... I can't take it
when Manny's fighting.

447
00:25:47,164 --> 00:25:48,540
I wait until it's over.

448
00:25:49,207 --> 00:25:50,584
Was anybody with you?

449
00:25:50,959 --> 00:25:54,463
Yes. Plenty of people.
There's always people around.

450
00:25:55,630 --> 00:25:57,007
But yeah, you know what?

451
00:25:57,299 --> 00:25:59,384
I could have sneaked off
and killed the lady...

452
00:26:00,010 --> 00:26:02,179
Only I didn't.
We done?

453
00:26:03,055 --> 00:26:04,431
For now.

454
00:26:06,683 --> 00:26:08,060
- Bea, come on.
- No, no, no.

455
00:26:08,185 --> 00:26:09,561
- Don't be mad.
- Not here.

456
00:26:10,604 --> 00:26:12,189
You wanna talk to Floyd Benton.

457
00:26:12,481 --> 00:26:14,024
The lady was gonna write
about how he dopes

458
00:26:14,149 --> 00:26:15,525
his young fighters at his gym.

459
00:26:16,234 --> 00:26:17,611
That's why we took
Manny out of there.

460
00:26:18,403 --> 00:26:20,322
Where were you the night
of the Flacco/Merriman fight?

461
00:26:20,530 --> 00:26:23,909
At the fight. I had to buy a ticket.
You believe that?

462
00:26:24,451 --> 00:26:27,370
Charlotte Mitchell asked you about steroid
use at your gym, correct?

463
00:26:28,830 --> 00:26:30,207
Beatriz Flacco.

464
00:26:30,582 --> 00:26:33,502
She hasn't liked me since
she was a little girl in pigtails.

465
00:26:33,794 --> 00:26:35,587
What's Beatriz Flacco
got to do with this?

466
00:26:35,712 --> 00:26:38,757
- She told you that crap.
- We heard from numerous sources

467
00:26:38,882 --> 00:26:40,550
that Flacco fired you as his trainer

468
00:26:40,675 --> 00:26:42,094
because you were pushing
steroids on him.

469
00:26:42,219 --> 00:26:46,056
- No one was pushed to do anything.
- But there was steroid abuse

470
00:26:46,181 --> 00:26:47,641
and Charlotte found out
about it, right?

471
00:26:48,308 --> 00:26:51,394
Big scoop. Athletes get juiced.

472
00:26:51,853 --> 00:26:53,230
Steroid abuse is a crime.

473
00:26:54,106 --> 00:26:55,857
So arrest me. I won't resist.

474
00:26:56,983 --> 00:27:00,028
I've done far worse things
than abuse steroids.

475
00:27:00,445 --> 00:27:03,365
I wouldn't hurt a lady over
some picayune nonsense like...

476
00:27:04,074 --> 00:27:05,575
Steroids? Please.

477
00:27:08,495 --> 00:27:10,872
They all had motive,
and they all had opportunity.

478
00:27:12,624 --> 00:27:14,000
What about the notebooks?

479
00:27:14,126 --> 00:27:15,627
I read her last six months of notes.

480
00:27:15,752 --> 00:27:18,213
- There's nothing useful that I could see.
- Could I take a look?

481
00:27:18,839 --> 00:27:20,215
Be my guest.

482
00:27:33,562 --> 00:27:35,856
- Excuse me, agent.
- Mr. Reyes, what brings you here?

483
00:27:36,189 --> 00:27:38,316
Look, I just saw on TV
that that lady who died...

484
00:27:38,441 --> 00:27:39,818
Her father just had
a heart attack.

485
00:27:40,318 --> 00:27:42,779
- Now is he gonna be okay?
- I'm not sure yet. He's in I.C.U.

486
00:27:45,740 --> 00:27:47,117
What's up, Mr. Reyes?

487
00:27:48,201 --> 00:27:49,744
Look, I lied before.

488
00:27:50,829 --> 00:27:52,205
Take a seat.

489
00:27:55,417 --> 00:27:56,793
Thanks.

490
00:28:01,173 --> 00:28:02,549
Go ahead.

491
00:28:02,716 --> 00:28:04,426
When I told you I don't
see Dawn anymore

492
00:28:05,135 --> 00:28:07,637
well, I... I do... see her every
now and again.

493
00:28:07,888 --> 00:28:09,973
- You know, for old times' sake.
- Hey, why not?

494
00:28:11,266 --> 00:28:13,018
You people got me thinking
about that damn gun

495
00:28:13,143 --> 00:28:15,145
and all the mess it's caused,
so I went to see Dawn

496
00:28:15,770 --> 00:28:17,522
and she told me she told
you she gave that gun

497
00:28:17,647 --> 00:28:19,274
to her cousin Bobby, who passed.

498
00:28:19,441 --> 00:28:21,276
That's right. We can't track
the gun past him.

499
00:28:22,652 --> 00:28:24,279
Yeah, well, it's not true
what she said.

500
00:28:25,071 --> 00:28:27,157
She didn't gave that gun to Bobby,
God rest his soul.

501
00:28:27,782 --> 00:28:30,410
She just said that because Bobby's dead
and he can't deny it, you know?

502
00:28:30,911 --> 00:28:33,580
- She didn't wanna get into trouble.
- What did she do with the gun?

503
00:28:40,754 --> 00:28:43,340
Frank Lopez. We need to talk to you.

504
00:28:45,342 --> 00:28:49,137
CBI? I ain't never been
questioned by the CBI.

505
00:28:49,846 --> 00:28:51,223
Guys...

506
00:28:52,432 --> 00:28:53,808
Thank you.

507
00:28:58,021 --> 00:28:59,397
What you got?

508
00:28:59,522 --> 00:29:00,899
Ten years ago,
a woman named Dawn May

509
00:29:01,066 --> 00:29:02,525
- gave you a 9-millimeter handgun.
- She did?

510
00:29:02,734 --> 00:29:04,694
- You still have the weapon?
- Why do you ask?

511
00:29:04,819 --> 00:29:06,446
Well, the gun was used
in a murder two days ago.

512
00:29:06,988 --> 00:29:08,365
Oops.

513
00:29:08,907 --> 00:29:10,283
Dawn May.

514
00:29:11,368 --> 00:29:13,828
The name's not ringing any bells.
What kind of gun was it?

515
00:29:15,163 --> 00:29:16,539
9-millimeter.

516
00:29:17,582 --> 00:29:20,293
Oh, yeah! Yeah,
it was a nice weapon. A Glock.

517
00:29:21,461 --> 00:29:22,837
Yeah, Dawn.

518
00:29:22,963 --> 00:29:25,507
Skinny, crazy girl.
What happened to Dawn?

519
00:29:25,632 --> 00:29:27,217
Oh, she's fine.
And the Glock?

520
00:29:27,634 --> 00:29:29,219
- Oh, I lost it.
- You lost it.

521
00:29:29,970 --> 00:29:32,973
Yeah. Four years ago...
At a club called, uh...

522
00:29:33,306 --> 00:29:34,683
Narcissus. You know it?

523
00:29:34,849 --> 00:29:36,893
There was a scuffle.
I had to run out after some punk.

524
00:29:37,018 --> 00:29:38,812
Next time I look, the 9 was gone.

525
00:29:39,646 --> 00:29:41,398
It's a nice weapon,
but what can you do?

526
00:29:42,107 --> 00:29:43,984
And, uh, where were you
two nights ago?

527
00:29:47,737 --> 00:29:49,698
I was here.
Any one of these guys will tell you.

528
00:29:50,740 --> 00:29:53,285
You don't believe me?
You can lie-detect me.

529
00:29:53,952 --> 00:29:55,328
I ain't worried.

530
00:30:02,585 --> 00:30:03,962
What'd you get?

531
00:30:04,087 --> 00:30:06,715
That guy LaRoche... He wants
to talk to me wants me to come in.

532
00:30:06,923 --> 00:30:08,300
What'd he talk to you about?

533
00:30:08,508 --> 00:30:11,094
Okay, look, uh,
I have to tell you something.

534
00:30:12,554 --> 00:30:14,139
I should've told
you before, but I didn't.

535
00:30:15,515 --> 00:30:17,058
Two years ago, my dad called me

536
00:30:17,309 --> 00:30:19,769
and he was getting hit
with a parole violation.

537
00:30:20,353 --> 00:30:21,980
Seen consorting
with known criminals

538
00:30:22,814 --> 00:30:24,816
and he was looking at a full
20-year bit in Folsom.

539
00:30:25,358 --> 00:30:27,027
- So you alibied him out.
- Yeah.

540
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:29,821
I said he was with me
at the time, but...

541
00:30:31,072 --> 00:30:32,449
I'm family.

542
00:30:32,574 --> 00:30:34,242
So the parole officer wanted to know
if there was anybody else there

543
00:30:34,367 --> 00:30:38,455
you know, who could verify it,
and... I said you.

544
00:30:39,873 --> 00:30:42,167
- What?
- It just came out of my mouth.

545
00:30:42,292 --> 00:30:44,002
I swear to God, if I could've taken it back,
I would've.

546
00:30:44,127 --> 00:30:45,879
But they never checked
back with you

547
00:30:46,004 --> 00:30:48,673
and everything seemed fine,
so I just forgot about it

548
00:30:48,798 --> 00:30:50,216
until LaRoche started
questioning me.

549
00:30:50,342 --> 00:30:52,802
So you involved me in your perjury
and now P.S.U. is investigating it.

550
00:30:52,927 --> 00:30:55,263
If LaRoche finds out about this,
my career is over.

551
00:30:55,388 --> 00:30:58,350
Yeah, it is, unless I lie as well
back you up, right?

552
00:30:58,558 --> 00:31:00,477
Look, I'm sorry, man.
I know I've put you in a bad spot.

553
00:31:01,895 --> 00:31:03,271
I've been a cop close to ten years.

554
00:31:03,480 --> 00:31:05,774
Never lied to another cop,
not once.

555
00:31:06,816 --> 00:31:08,401
Look, I'm not asking
for you to lie now.

556
00:31:08,943 --> 00:31:11,237
I just... I want you to do
what you think is right.

557
00:31:13,156 --> 00:31:14,532
Yeah.

558
00:31:25,251 --> 00:31:26,628
So what are you gonna do?

559
00:31:28,421 --> 00:31:29,798
I'm not lying for you.

560
00:31:30,256 --> 00:31:31,800
"Manny Flacco will be fighting"

561
00:31:31,925 --> 00:31:34,761
"for the middleweight crown
on Cinco de Mayo."

562
00:31:35,011 --> 00:31:37,305
"It will be a second
American revolution."

563
00:31:37,555 --> 00:31:38,932
"What a country."

564
00:31:39,057 --> 00:31:40,850
"Where else can a kid
from the barrio"

565
00:31:41,017 --> 00:31:42,811
"and a son of Armenian immigrants"

566
00:31:43,103 --> 00:31:45,313
"come together to make something
like this happen?"

567
00:31:45,522 --> 00:31:49,025
{\an8}"Me, a guy, who five years ago,
owned a few parking lots"

568
00:31:49,150 --> 00:31:51,403
{\an8}"and a couple of restaurants
and nightclubs?"

569
00:31:51,528 --> 00:31:53,655
{\an8}"And a kid who never graduated
high school."

570
00:31:53,947 --> 00:31:57,617
{\an8}"But we had a dream, and today
that dream is a reality.

571
00:31:58,034 --> 00:31:59,411
"God bless America."

572
00:32:00,995 --> 00:32:03,415
- Anything on Mitchell's notes?
- Not a thing.

573
00:32:04,165 --> 00:32:06,501
Manny Flacco is challenging
for the middleweight crown.

574
00:32:06,626 --> 00:32:08,753
- Len Artash just announced it.
- What are you doing?

575
00:32:09,003 --> 00:32:10,630
Going to talk to Len Artash.
You coming?

576
00:32:14,300 --> 00:32:15,677
Pull the guard!

577
00:32:16,261 --> 00:32:17,971
Reverse, reverse, reverse.

578
00:32:19,472 --> 00:32:21,975
- Watch the guillotine!
- Artash, got some questions for you.

579
00:32:22,100 --> 00:32:24,394
- You were born in America, yes?
- That's right.

580
00:32:24,519 --> 00:32:27,564
- And your parents are Armenian.
- Yes. Why?

581
00:32:27,689 --> 00:32:30,275
- What was your father's name?
- Arik Artashian.

582
00:32:30,442 --> 00:32:32,610
- What's your father's name?
- Floyd.

583
00:32:33,236 --> 00:32:34,612
And your mother?

584
00:32:35,321 --> 00:32:37,157
Nancy. What is this about?

585
00:32:37,615 --> 00:32:39,617
Nancy... doesn't sound
like an Armenian name.

586
00:32:40,076 --> 00:32:43,455
No, it's not. It's what she called herself
when she got here to America.

587
00:32:43,621 --> 00:32:46,166
- What was she christened?
- Nargiz.

588
00:32:46,499 --> 00:32:48,418
- And do you have...
- Nargiz.

589
00:32:49,085 --> 00:32:52,505
- I bet that means something beautiful.
- It's a flower.

590
00:32:52,797 --> 00:32:54,174
Either of you recognize this?

591
00:32:55,884 --> 00:32:57,260
No. What is it?

592
00:32:57,510 --> 00:32:58,887
It's Charlotte
Mitchell's notebook.

593
00:32:59,012 --> 00:33:00,388
You know what that says?

594
00:33:02,974 --> 00:33:04,476
- What about you?
- No.

595
00:33:05,310 --> 00:33:06,686
- What do you think it is?
- I don't know.

596
00:33:06,811 --> 00:33:09,397
Some kind of coded shorthand,
most likely.

597
00:33:09,939 --> 00:33:13,485
Doesn't matter. I'll bet her father
knows what it says.

598
00:33:14,110 --> 00:33:16,654
Doctors said that Thomas Mitchell
has taken a turn for the better.

599
00:33:17,113 --> 00:33:20,033
Expected to regain consciousness
in 12 to 24 hours, right?

600
00:33:20,283 --> 00:33:21,659
- Right.
- Right, so there we have it.

601
00:33:21,784 --> 00:33:23,411
Thomas Mitchell will tell us
what this says

602
00:33:23,995 --> 00:33:26,873
and then I'll bet we will find out what
Charlotte learned that got her killed.

603
00:33:30,126 --> 00:33:33,171
I went through that entire notebook.
There wasn't any shorthand in it.

604
00:33:33,296 --> 00:33:36,090
Really? How weird.
Wonder where it came from.

605
00:33:49,936 --> 00:33:53,356
You served in the military
didn't you, agent Cho?

606
00:33:56,317 --> 00:33:57,693
Yes.

607
00:33:57,860 --> 00:34:01,280
- Rangers?
- Special Forces.

608
00:34:03,699 --> 00:34:07,537
So... you understand
the concept of honor.

609
00:34:12,500 --> 00:34:14,669
That's an affidavit
that Wayne Rigsby signed

610
00:34:15,836 --> 00:34:18,256
saying that you and he spent
an afternoon

611
00:34:18,756 --> 00:34:20,132
with his criminal father.

612
00:34:21,509 --> 00:34:23,386
You remember that day, agent Cho?

613
00:34:30,977 --> 00:34:35,273
Agent Rigsby initially claimed
to have no contact with his father

614
00:34:35,940 --> 00:34:39,443
then became evasive when confronted
with his falsehood.

615
00:34:44,865 --> 00:34:48,411
Looking into it,
I... discovered that...

616
00:34:49,537 --> 00:34:52,623
Wayne provided an alibi
that kept his father out of jail...

617
00:34:55,167 --> 00:34:56,794
And you were part of that alibi.

618
00:35:00,590 --> 00:35:01,966
So...

619
00:35:03,426 --> 00:35:07,597
I just need you to confirm...

620
00:35:09,974 --> 00:35:11,350
On your honor...

621
00:35:12,768 --> 00:35:14,270
That you were indeed
there that day.

622
00:35:18,107 --> 00:35:19,483
Yes, I was.

623
00:35:20,443 --> 00:35:22,403
I was there with agent Rigsby
and his father.

624
00:35:23,821 --> 00:35:25,197
Okay.

625
00:35:25,823 --> 00:35:27,199
Good.

626
00:35:35,166 --> 00:35:37,251
What did you do that afternoon...

627
00:35:38,210 --> 00:35:39,587
The three of you?

628
00:35:40,129 --> 00:35:41,505
Give me some details.

629
00:35:45,468 --> 00:35:46,844
I don't recall.

630
00:35:51,474 --> 00:35:52,850
Nothing at all?

631
00:35:53,893 --> 00:35:55,269
Strange.

632
00:35:55,436 --> 00:35:56,812
I was there.

633
00:35:57,396 --> 00:35:58,773
I'll swear to it.

634
00:35:59,774 --> 00:36:01,359
You need me to sign something
to make it official?

635
00:36:03,778 --> 00:36:05,154
No.

636
00:36:06,155 --> 00:36:07,531
That won't be necessary.

637
00:36:15,498 --> 00:36:18,292
That'll be all. Thank you, agent.

638
00:36:30,471 --> 00:36:31,847
I told him I was with you.

639
00:36:32,390 --> 00:36:34,058
All right, let's go.
We've gotta get to the hospital.

640
00:36:34,183 --> 00:36:36,769
Jane and Van Pelt are already there.
You guys okay?

641
00:36:38,604 --> 00:36:40,314
Let's go. I'll explain on the way.

642
00:36:46,278 --> 00:36:47,655
All clear in Mitchell's room.

643
00:36:51,826 --> 00:36:53,202
Hallway's clear.

644
00:36:53,661 --> 00:36:55,037
All clear here.

645
00:36:58,082 --> 00:36:59,458
Wait a minute.

646
00:37:01,043 --> 00:37:02,670
I think I saw Reyes.
He's headed your way.

647
00:37:12,763 --> 00:37:14,181
I see him, Cho.
Cut him off.

648
00:37:21,105 --> 00:37:22,481
Mr. Reyes.

649
00:37:22,606 --> 00:37:23,983
What are you doing here?

650
00:37:24,108 --> 00:37:25,568
Um, I was just coming
to pay my respects.

651
00:37:25,693 --> 00:37:27,153
No, you can't be here.
We have to leave now.

652
00:37:27,278 --> 00:37:28,904
Wait. I didn't mean anything.
What are you doing?

653
00:37:29,029 --> 00:37:30,865
Don't argue, Mr. Reyes.
Right this way. Come on.

654
00:38:08,611 --> 00:38:11,238
Mr. Lima, put your hands on
your head where I can see 'em.

655
00:38:12,114 --> 00:38:13,741
Mr. Mitchell left the I.C.U. yesterday

656
00:38:13,908 --> 00:38:15,951
but I'll be glad to pass
on your best wishes.

657
00:38:16,327 --> 00:38:18,078
Whatever. You got nothing.

658
00:38:18,913 --> 00:38:21,040
That notebook shorthand
crap won't fly in court.

659
00:38:21,165 --> 00:38:25,711
True enough. I happened to write
that notebook shorthand crap myself.

660
00:38:26,545 --> 00:38:29,340
Charlotte Mitchell was murdered
because she discovered a secret.

661
00:38:29,715 --> 00:38:31,091
I simply had to convince the killer

662
00:38:31,258 --> 00:38:34,178
that the secret didn't die with her.
Et voila.

663
00:38:34,970 --> 00:38:36,639
And this should fly
nicely in court.

664
00:38:36,889 --> 00:38:38,265
- You got it all wrong...
- Save it.

665
00:38:38,557 --> 00:38:40,893
This is the gun that was used
to shoot Charlotte Mitchell

666
00:38:41,018 --> 00:38:42,394
and you're the one who killed her.

667
00:38:48,984 --> 00:38:50,653
You can have these back now,
Mr. Mitchell.

668
00:38:52,363 --> 00:38:53,739
I, uh...

669
00:38:54,198 --> 00:38:56,033
I'm sorry,
but I... I scribbled in one of those.

670
00:38:56,158 --> 00:38:58,994
That's, uh, how we caught the man
that shot your daughter.

671
00:38:59,495 --> 00:39:01,914
- I hope you don't mind.
- No, no. That's, uh...

672
00:39:03,332 --> 00:39:06,502
So... um, it's over?

673
00:39:07,711 --> 00:39:10,297
- You've solved the case?
- Yes.

674
00:39:10,798 --> 00:39:12,341
Now we're just tying up
some loose ends.

675
00:39:17,638 --> 00:39:21,559
Never... never would've figured
Suge Lima as a murderer.

676
00:39:22,184 --> 00:39:23,561
Yeah, that's terrible.

677
00:39:24,186 --> 00:39:26,063
- Shocking.
- Yes, it is.

678
00:39:27,064 --> 00:39:29,441
What for? Why did he do it?

679
00:39:30,067 --> 00:39:33,445
So, uh... is there anything
I can do to help?

680
00:39:33,779 --> 00:39:35,155
There is, actually.

681
00:39:35,281 --> 00:39:38,784
- Your... your mother's name... the flower?
- Yes. Nargiz.

682
00:39:38,909 --> 00:39:42,246
Nargiz, which means...
Narcissus...

683
00:39:42,454 --> 00:39:45,291
Same name as your club
named it after your mom.

684
00:39:45,708 --> 00:39:48,127
- Yeah.
- Club Narcissus

685
00:39:48,419 --> 00:39:51,380
where Frank Lopez
lost Joe Reyes' gun.

686
00:39:51,505 --> 00:39:52,882
Yeah, the one
he got from Dawn May.

687
00:39:53,215 --> 00:39:56,260
- That one.
- Who? What?

688
00:39:56,385 --> 00:39:59,013
You don't know the guys,
but we know how you got the gun

689
00:39:59,138 --> 00:40:02,433
that Lima used to kill Charlotte Mitchell
and you're under arrest. Stand up.

690
00:40:02,933 --> 00:40:04,852
The only thing we don't know
is why you had to kill her.

691
00:40:05,227 --> 00:40:06,604
And that's what we're gonna find out.

692
00:40:10,649 --> 00:40:13,736
Mr. Flacco, do you remember
around a year ago

693
00:40:13,861 --> 00:40:15,237
giving blood to be tested?

694
00:40:15,613 --> 00:40:18,490
Sure. Results came back
said I was as healthy as a horse.

695
00:40:18,741 --> 00:40:20,117
Suge told me.

696
00:40:20,910 --> 00:40:22,286
Suge lied.

697
00:40:23,579 --> 00:40:25,372
He and Artash
submitted the samples

698
00:40:25,497 --> 00:40:28,000
under Suge's name instead
of yours just in case.

699
00:40:29,001 --> 00:40:30,794
Markers showed
a high level of protein

700
00:40:30,920 --> 00:40:33,964
that indicates cranial
bleeding and spinal leakage.

701
00:40:34,632 --> 00:40:36,008
Oh, my God.

702
00:40:37,801 --> 00:40:39,637
Charlotte Mitchell
figured out the switch.

703
00:40:43,641 --> 00:40:45,517
I know that blood sample
was Manny's, not Lima's.

704
00:40:46,060 --> 00:40:47,770
If Manny gets in that cage,
he could die.

705
00:40:48,228 --> 00:40:50,064
What the hell are you
talking about, lady?

706
00:40:50,648 --> 00:40:52,608
And how'd you get your hands
on those tests?

707
00:40:52,858 --> 00:40:54,610
Stop the fight, Len, or else.

708
00:40:55,527 --> 00:40:59,031
All right, all right.
I'll stop the fight. Calm down.

709
00:41:02,952 --> 00:41:04,328
We got a problem.

710
00:41:08,916 --> 00:41:10,626
Those sons of bitches.

711
00:41:11,669 --> 00:41:13,128
They risked Manny's life.

712
00:41:13,337 --> 00:41:16,423
No M.M.A. authority would let him
in the cage if word got out.

713
00:41:22,429 --> 00:41:24,431
It's one doctor's opinion.
He looks fine to me.

714
00:41:24,848 --> 00:41:26,600
Do you really think
you'll get away with this?

715
00:41:27,142 --> 00:41:28,519
I will tell everyone.

716
00:41:29,353 --> 00:41:30,729
Let go of me.

717
00:41:30,938 --> 00:41:32,314
Let go of me.

718
00:41:32,439 --> 00:41:33,816
Let go of me.

719
